+    /// The frame last_write_frame, CheckCrossFrameUse and RelocationCandidate's same-frame rule
+    /// count in. frame_tick advances at the composite, a sync request the back serves wherever it
+    /// is, so one host tick holds the end of one guest frame and the start of the next
+    /// (fable_answer_16 1a). With the render-frame clock (FritchiiRenderClock: always with
+    /// EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_RELOCATE) it follows Tegra::g_nx2_render_frame instead (bumped where the
+    /// frame's last GPU work is), falling back to frame_tick while that does not advance.
+    /// Monotonic across the switches; the LRU, the collector and the logs keep frame_tick.
+    /// Without the clock it is frame_tick.
+    [[nodiscard]] u64 RenderFrame() const noexcept {
+        const u64 source = render_clock_live ? Tegra::Nx2RenderFrameCount() : frame_tick;
+        return render_clock_base + (source - render_clock_source_base);
+    }
+    /// Whether a relocation may trust "not written in this frame" now, and that frame's number
+    /// (one read of the counter, used for the whole decision). Only while the clock is live (not
