+    /// render_frame (RelocationBoundary's), a drift of less than its size, nothing unusual about
+    /// it (sparse, converted, aliased, remapped, rescaled, CPU-read, a download queued, bound as
+    /// another target of this clear by slot or by rt_control's map, a smaller target bound,
+    /// registered in another channel). Else none.
